  "interpretation": "2.6 A is the best-F1 point (0.9888) and is the cutoff the cohort builder already writes labels with, so the decoder default was moved 2.5 -> 2.6. The element filter is the larger error term: even at the perfect distance the pre-Wf-A94 set can only reach 55.6% of true Pt bonds; halides lift that to 75.1%. The remaining 24.9% is Pt-C (396), Pt-As (15), Pt-B (8), Pt-Si (5) - covalent/organometallic bonds, left OUT of the donor set deliberately because 'dative candidate' would then fire on every Pt-C contact.",
